268:\begin{definition}[\textbf{Polynomial equivalence relation}, {\cite[Def. 3.1]{BodlaenderJK14}}]
269:Given an alphabet $\Sigma$, an equivalence relation $\mathcal{R}$ on $\Sigma^\star$ is called a polynomial equivalence relation if the following conditions hold.
271:\item There is an algorithm that, given two strings $x, y \in \Sigma^ \star$, decides whether $x$
272:and $y$ belong to the same equivalence class in time polynomial in $|x| + |y|$.
274:\item For any finite set $S \subseteq \Sigma^ \star$ the equivalence relation $\mathcal{R}$ partitions the elements of $S$ into a number of classes that is polynomially bounded in the size of the largest element of $S$.
